irection inferred from FX data below: mixed.\n- COP: 3,100/USD \u2014 a 7-year high (strong peso) [Estimate, medellin.co, 2026-07-31]. BBVA forecasts COP average 3,628 in 2026 and 3,698 in 2027 [Estimate, BBVA Research June 2026] \u2192 implies significant future depreciation (headwind for USD-reported earnings).\n- Inflation: still a constraint; Fed on hold due to inflation concerns [Actual, J.P. Morgan]\n- Credit spreads: not retrieved; investment-grade retail funding conditions normal [Unconfirmed]\n\nStep 1-2. Regime Probability Distribution\n- Goldilocks: 25% \u2014 hard to sustain with 10Y at 4.71%\n- Reflation: 35% \u2014 high rates + positive growth; current best fit\n- Stagflation: 20% \u2014 LatAm FX/ Inflation pressures\n- Total = 100%\n\nStep 1-3. Macro Sensitivity (each -3 to +3)\n- Interest rates: -1 (low debt; membership model resilient)\n- Dollar: -3 (USD reporting; strong USD hurts translation; COP is 20%+ of sales)\n- Liquidity: -1 (EM consumer discretionary within staples)\n- Economic cycle: -2 (LatAm consumer exposed to EM cycles)\n- Commodity: +1 (food inflation lifts comps but can squeeze margins; net slight positive)\n\nStep 1-4. Macro Alignment: HEADWIND (-0.5 conv.) \u2014 driven by the dollar/COP axis, not by rates.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 1.5. BASE RATE & HISTORICAL PATTERN\n\nStep 1.5-1. Base Rates\n- 5-yr survival of a profitable public retailer: ~85-90% [Assumption] \u2192 PSMT-specific: ~95% (net-cash balance sheet, 57 clubs) [Estimate]\n- Narrow-moat regional retailer doubling earnings in 5 years: ~25-35% [Assumption] \u2192 PSMT evidence (record renewals, +12.5% Q3 comp, 6 club pipeline) raises to ~45% [Estimate]\n- Operating margin expansion by >100bp over 5 years for mature retailers: ~30% [Assumption] \u2192 PSMT (membership at 35.8% of op. income, fee increases) \u2192 ~40% [Estimate]\n- Chile new-market success (5-yr breakeven): base ~50% for established operators [Assumption]\n\nStep 1.5-2. Deviation from Base Rate: Base case revenue CAGR of 8-10% exceeds the 5-7% base rate for mature retail. Justified by: (1) 6 new clubs in 18 months, taking club count from 57 to 63 = ~7-8% unit growth [Actual, company IR]; (2) Colombia comp strength (+30.5% reported / +13.8% cc) [Actual, company presentation via research brief]; (3) 4M cardholders with record renewal [Actual, IR]. Sufficient justification.\n\nStep 1.5-3. Base Rate Shock: My base success probability (earnings ~2.2x by FY30) is 2.2x the 25-35% base rate \u2014 RED FLAG. Requires the revenue/margin assumptions above; margin expansion beyond 5.0% would require 2.5x base rate \u2192 rejected.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\nStep 2-1. Business: PSMT is the only membership-warehouse operator in Central America, the Caribbean, and Colombia, running 57 clubs in 12 countries + 1 U.S. territory for 4M+ cardholders. It monetizes via merchandise margin + an annuity-like membership-fee stream (\u22481.5% of net merchandise sales but 35.8% of operating income, FY23) [Actual, 10-K]. Understandability: HIGH.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat Score (0-21): Intangibles 2, Switching costs 2, Network effects 0, Cost advantage 2, Economies of scale 2, Regulatory barriers 1, Data moat 1 \u2192 TOTAL 10/21 = NARROW MOAT. Direction: WIDENING (record renewal rates, market share improving 17.4\u219217.7% in key segments [Estimate, research brief]; private label growth).\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch: FAST GROWER (10%+ revenue growth; EPS growth ~15% consensus) with Stalwart traits.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard\n- Revenue CAGR (5-yr): +10.5% [Actual, arithmetic]\n- Operating margin: 4.4% TTM vs 4.5% 12-yr median [Actual]\n- ROE: 12.3% vendor / 12.5% arithmetic FY25 [Actual/Arithmetic]\n- ROIC: ~11.8% (NOPAT $149M / invested capital $1.26B) [Estimate]\n- FCF conversion: TTM FCF $73M / NI $160M = 46% (pre-SBC) [Arithmetic]\n- Net debt: ~$0.015B net debt (all debt incl. operating leases $0.329B minus cash $0.241B minus STI $0.073B) [Estimate \u2014 see Section 2.5]\n- Grade: GOOD (excellent balance sheet; weak FCF conversion during capex phase)\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation: Buybacks 1/3 (net issuance +0.1%/yr \u2014 no buybacks [Actual]); M&A 2/3 (no record; organic only); Capex efficiency 2/3 (incremental ROIC ~12-15% [Estimate]); Mix rationality 3/3 (high-sync growth capex); Guidance accuracy 2/3. Insider ownership 7.42% \u2192 +1. Total = 10/15 + 1 = 11/15. GOOD.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 2.5. INTANGIBLES-ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\n- R&D: N/A (retailer) \u2014 no adjustment.\n- SBC: FY25 $19M [Actual, Section 5]. Adjusted FCF = Reported FCF \u2212 SBC. TTM adjusted FCF = $73M \u2212 $20M \u2248 $53M [Arithmetic].\n- Operating leases: FY25 $130M [Actual, Section 6B]. Vendor total-debt scalar $329M equals the sum of LT debt ($148M) + current portion ($39M) + short-term borrowings ($12M) + operating leases ($130M) \u2014 suggesting 