on: club base grows, Chile contributes, FX mean-reverts].\n- Operating margin: 4.45% TTM [Actual, vendor/arithmetic]; FY27 dip (Chile startup) [Assumption]; expansion to 5.2% by FY33 via membership mix/operating leverage [Assumption \u2014 NOT guided; this is the key variable].\n- Tax rate: 36% [Estimate, derived from FY23: op inc $185M / NI $109M / interest $11M; LatAm statutory rates 25-35%].\n- Capex: FY26 $220M, FY27 $240M [Assumption: TTM capex is already $201M [Actual]; 6 new clubs incl. Chile land/DC]; normalize to $175M by FY33 [Assumption].\n- D&A: grows with PP&E ~8%/yr from FY25 $88M [Actual].\n- \u0394WC: 0 base case [Assumption \u2014 12-yr cumulative \u0394WC \u2248 +$150M \u2248 1.4% of cumulative sales [Arithmetic]].\n- SBC: from FY25 $19M [Actual], grows ~10%/yr [Assumption].\n\nStep 3-2. WACC Derivation\n- Rf: 4.71% (10Y UST, 2026-08-21) [Actual]\n- Beta: 0.90 [Estimate \u2014 vendor 0.787 [Aggregator] adjusted upward for EM sovereign/FX risk]\n- ERP: 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran EM range 4.5-5.5%]\n- CoE = 4.71% + 0.90 \u00d7 4.75% = 8.99%\n- CoD pre-tax: 5.75% [Assumption, ~105bp over 10Y]; after-tax 3.7%\n- Weights: E $5.379B / D $0.329B \u2192 D/(D+E) = 5.8%\n- WACC = 0.942 \u00d7 8.99% + 0.058 \u00d7 3.70% = 8.7% [Estimate]\n\nStep 3-3. DCF Valuation\n- Terminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 below LatAm USD nominal GDP, consistent with mature club base]. Terminal FCF = $259M \u00d7 1.03 = $267M.\n- TV = $267M / (8.7% \u2212 3.0%) = $4.68B.\n- PV of explicit FCFs (discount 1.087^1..8): 21+21+66+89+105+119+128+133 = $0.68B.\n- PV of TV = $4.68B / 1.087^8 = $2.40B.\n- EV = $3.08B; minus net debt $15M = equity $3.07B; / 30.86M shares = $99.5 \u2248 $100/share.\n\nStep 3-4. Cross-Checks (no single-method reliance)\n- FY30 EPS $8.35 [Arithmetic] \u00d7 20x mature-staples multiple = $167 in FY30; PV at 10% = $104. [Assumption]\n- Normalized FCF yield: FY30 FCF $160M / 4.2% fair yield = $3.8B \u2192 PV at 8.7% (5 yrs) = $2.5B \u2192 $81/share.