ly succeed ~70%\n    [Estimate \u2014 high-level generalisation; not sourced]\n  - Large-scale multi-country retail expansion beating ROIC>WACC:\n    ~50\u201360%  [Estimate]\n\nStep 1.5-2. Deviation of Current Analysis from Base Rate\n  My success probability in the Base Case (operating a stable,\n  profitable LatAm club operator growing at 6\u201310%) is ~80\u201385%.\n  This is within / only slightly above the base rate of ~85\u201390%.\n  Justifications for not reverting further toward base rate:\n  1) 12 consecutive years of positive net income and positive OCF\n     in the data pack \u2014 no loss year in the sample [Actual]\n  2) Membership renewal 90.5% all-time high at May 31, 2026 \u2014\n     recurring-revenue anchor [Actual \u2014 Q3 FY2026 transcript]\n  3) Colombia +30.5% USD / +13.8% constant-currency growth \u2014\n     proven expansion formula [Actual \u2014 Q2 FY2026 transcript]\n  No base-rate red flag.\n\nStep 1.5-3. Base Rate Shock Check\n  Success probability (80\u201385%) vs base rate (85%) \u2192 ratio ~1.0.\n  No red flag.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2. BUSINESS QUALITY\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nStep 2-1. Business Understanding\n  PriceSmart operates membership warehouse clubs in Central America,\n  Colombia and the Caribbean \u2014 selling food, fresh proteins, nonfood\n  merchandise and services (optical, pharmacy, food court), with\n  membership fees as a high-margin recurring revenue layer.\n  It charges $35\u2013$80+ per year, has 2.08M+ member accounts, and its\n  model depends on volume purchasing, private label (26.6% adjusted\n  penetration) and local-market logistics.\n  Understandability: HIGH.\n\nStep 2-2. Moat Assessment\n  Moat Type                        Score (0-3)\n  Intangible Assets (Brand)         2\n  Switching Costs                   2\n  Network Effects                   1\n  Cost Advantage                    2\n  Economies of Scale                2\n  Regulatory Barriers               1\n  Data Moat                         1\n  TOTAL                            \u200b11 / 21 \u2192 WIDE MOAT (low end)\n\n  Moat Direction: STABLE-TO-WIDENING.\n  Evidence: renewal rate 90.5% (record); Platinum mix up to 19.5% of\n  accounts from 14.5%; private label +50bps to 26.6%; digital sales\n  +23.4% to $94.1M.  [Actual \u2014 Q2/Q3 FY2026 transcripts]\n\nStep 2-3. Lynch Classification\n  STALWART with growth tilt.\n  Checkpoints: P/E 34.6x is well above its 10% growth rate\n  (PEG 1.83) \u2014 a Stalwart quality issue.  The market is pricing\n  this like a Fast Grower; the business is not growing earnings\n  at 25%+.\n\nStep 2-4. Financial Strength Scorecard\n  Revenue CAGR FY2020\u2013FY2025:         10.5%  [Actual \u2014 pack Section 7]\n  TTM revenue growth:                 ~12.1% [Arithmetic on pack quarterly]\n  Operating margin (12-yr median):    4.5%   [Actual \u2014 pack Section 7]\n  OPM FY2025:                         4.4%   [Actual \u2014 0.233/5.270]\n  Net income growth FY2024\u2192FY2025:    +6.5%  [Arithmetic \u2014 0.148/0.139]\n  TTM EPS:                            $5.04  [Arithmetic \u2014 0.160/0.03086]\n  ROE (FY2025):                       11.9%  [Arithmetic \u2014 0.148/1.247]\n  ROIC (FY2025E):                     ~13.6% [Estimate \u2014 NOPAT 0.172 /\n                                           IC ~1.26 incl. op leases]\n  FCF margin FY2025:                  2.0%   [Arithmetic \u2014 0.103/5.270]\n  FCF conversion (FCF/OCF):           39.5%  [Arithmetic]\n  Net debt (operating leases incl.):~$0.665B [Estimate \u2014 full debt calc]\n  Net debt / EBITDA:                 ~0.05x (excl. leases)  [Estimate]\n  Interest coverage:                 ~16.8x (FY2025 OI/interest)\n                                           [Arithmetic \u2014 OI 0.233 / 0.011]\n  Verdict: GOOD \u2014 low leverage, stable margins, positive earnings\n  history; but FCF conversion is WEAK (capex-heavy growth phase).\n\nStep 2-5. Capital Allocation Scorecard\n  1. Buyback efficiency:             0/3 \u2014 no buybacks; net issuance +0.1%/yr\n  2. M&A track record:               1/3 \u2014 no major M&A to evaluate\n  3. Capex efficiency:               2/3 \u2014 incremental ROIC ~16% (good)\n  4. Rationality of mix:             2/3 \u2014 growth capex + growing dividend;\n     reasonable, no excess cash hoarding\n  5. Guidance accuracy:              2/3 \u2014 mixed beats/misses (Q2 beat,\n     Q3 EPS miss)\n  Insider bonus:                     +1 (7.42% insider ownership)\n  TOTAL: 8/15  (above average but not exceptional)\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\n\u25a0 SECTION 2.5. ADJUSTED FINANCIALS\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nStep 2.5-1. R&D Capitalization\n  PSMT is a retailer; R&D is immaterial.  Technology/digital spend\n  is embedded in SG&A.  No adjustment.  [Assumption]\n\nStep 2.5-2. SBC Proper Treatment\n  FY2025 SBC: $0.019B [Actual \u2014 pack Section 5]\n  Adjusted FY2025 FCF: $0.103B \u2212 $0.019B = $0.084B [Arithmetic]\n  TTM adjusted FCF: $0.074B \u2212 ~$0.019B = ~$0.055B [Estimate]\n  Management treats SBC as expense-through-OCF add-back; I deduct it\n  as a real expense.\n\nStep 2.5-3. Operating Lease Capitalization\n  FY2025 operating leases: $0.130B [Actual \u2014 pack Section 6B]\n  Capitalized at 6\u00d7 rent [Assumption \u2014 retail standard]: $0.780B\n  Adjusted debt = 0.199B (LT+current+ST borrowings) + 0.780B = $0.979B\n  Adjusted net debt = 0.979 \u2212 0.241 cash \u2212 0.073 ST investments\n                     = $0.665B [Estimate]\n\nStep 2.5-4. Brand/Data Asset Estimation\n  Brand value: not quantified (owned club model, regional brand).\n  Data asset: 2.08M members \u00d7 74.7% online profiles = ~1.55M digital\n  profiles [Estimate]; digital sales $94.1M +23.4% \u2014 directional\n  value only.  No specific asset value booked.\n\nStep 2.5-5. Adjusted ROIC\n  Adjusted IC = GAAP IC (~$1.26B) + capitalized leases ($0.78B) +\n  unamortized R&D (~$0.05B) \u2248 $2.09B [Estimate]\n  Adjusted NOPAT \u2248 $0.172B (R&D adj immaterial)\n  Adjusted ROIC \u2248 8.2%\n  GAAP ROIC \u2248 13.6%\n  Gap: 5.4pp \u2014 explained entirely by lease capitalisation.\n  Verdict: economically acceptable but not exceptional.\n\nStep 2.5-6. Owner Earnings (Buffett-style)\n  Owner Earnings = NI + D&A \u2212 Maintenance Capex \u2212 \u0394WC\n                 = 0.148 + 0.088 \u2212 ~0.095 \u2212 0.096\n                 = $0.045B [Estimate]\n  The low owner-earnings number is the single most important data\n  point in this report: the business does not currently generate\n  meaningful owner cash after