on: 6 clubs \u2192 63; comps 5-7% cc; FX \u22121.5%]. FY29-33 taper 7.5%\u21924.0% [Assumption: club base grows, Chile contributes, FX mean-reverts].\n- Operating margin: 4.45% TTM [Actual, vendor/arithmetic]; FY27 dip (Chile startup) [Assumption]; expansion to 5.2% by FY33 via membership mix/operating leverage [Assumption \u2014 NOT guided; this is the key variable].\n- Tax rate: 36% [Estimate, derived from FY23: op inc $185M / NI $109M / interest $11M; LatAm statutory rates 25-35%].\n- Capex: FY26 $220M, FY27 $240M [Assumption: TTM capex is already $201M [Actual]; 6 new clubs incl. Chile land/DC]; normalize to $175M by FY33 [Assumption].\n- D&A: grows with PP&E ~8%/yr from FY25 $88M [Actual].\n- \u0394WC: 0 base case [Assumption \u2014 12-yr cumulative \u0394WC \u2248 +$150M \u2248 1.4% of cumulative sales [Arithmetic]].\n- SBC: from FY25 $19M [Actual], grows ~10%/yr [Assumption].\n\nStep 3-2. WACC Derivation\n- Rf: 4.71% (10Y UST, 2026-08-21) [Actual]\n- Beta: 0.90 [Estimate \u2014 vendor 0.787 [Aggregator] adjusted upward for EM sovereign/FX risk]\n- ERP: 4.75% [Assumption \u2014 Damodaran EM range 4.5-5.5%]\n- CoE = 4.71% + 0.90 \u00d7 4.75% = 8.99%\n- CoD pre-tax: 5.75% [Assumption, ~105bp over 10Y]; after-tax 3.7%\n- Weights: E $5.379B / D $0.329B \u2192 D/(D+E) = 5.8%\n- WACC = 0.942 \u00d7 8.99% + 0.058 \u00d7 3.70% = 8.7% [Estimate]\n\nStep 3-3. DCF Valuation\n- Terminal growth: 3.0% [Assumption \u2014 below LatAm USD nominal GDP, consistent with mature club base]. Terminal FCF = $259M \u00d7 1.03 = $267M.\n- TV = $267M / (8.7% \u2212 3.0%) = $4.68B.\n- PV of explicit FCFs (discount 1.087^1..8): 21+21+66+89+105+119+128+133 = $0.68B.\n- PV of TV = $4.68B / 1.087^8 = $2.40B.\n- EV = $3.08B; minus net debt $15M = equity $3.07B; / 30.86M shares = $99.5 \u2248 $100/share.\n\nStep 3-4. Cross-Checks (no single-method reliance)\n- FY30 EPS $8.35 [Arithmetic] \u00d7 20x mature-staples multiple = $167 in FY30; PV at 10% = $104. [Assumption]\n- Normalized FCF yield: FY30 FCF $160M / 4.2% fair yield = $3.8B \u2192 PV at 8.7% (5 yrs) = $2.5B \u2192 $81/share. [Assumption]\n- Sell-side: mean target $153.33, high $165 [Aggregator] \u2014 ALL BELOW T0 price.\n- Reverse DCF: T0 EV $5.39B minus PV of explicit FCFs $0.68B \u2192 required PV of TV = $4.71B \u2192 TV at yr 5 = $4.71\u00d71.087^5 = $7.15B \u2192 required terminal FCF = $7.15B \u00d7 5.7% = $408M. That is 1.8x my terminal FCF and implies FY31 operating income \u2248 $620M (vs $233M FY25) \u2014 a 2.7x increase. The market is paying for a margin-accelerating bull case at 8.7% discount; there is no cushion for disappointment.\n\nStep 3-5. Tornado Sensitivity (\u00b11\u03c3) \u2014 Top 3 variables\n1. FY33 operating margin (5.2% base; 4.5% / 6.0%): IV $88 / $128\n2. WACC (8.7% base; 9.5% / 7.9%): IV $92 / $115\n3. Terminal g (3.0% base; 2.0% / 4.0%): IV $93 / $113\nBase IV = $100-102. Thesis KPIs: FY26-28 operating margin; WACC/10Y; terminal growth.\n\n\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\u2550\nSECTION 3.5. SECOND-ORDER EFFECTS\n\n- Competitive response: If PSMT succeeds in Chile (2027), Walmart (Lider) and Cencosud will likely sharpen pricing. Counter-move impact: -2. Unlike Central America, Chile already has big-box competition [Estimate].\n- Reflexivity: Positive for bulls (higher price \u2192 SBC attraction, cheaper capital for Chile); Neutral-negative at T0 (price is above intrinsic \u2014 no operational reflexivity; PSMT does not use stock as currency).\n- Customer behavior: 4M cardholders, record renewals [Actual]; platinum membership penetration rising [Estimate]. As penetration grows, LTV rises but CAC rises in new markets (Chile)